chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "SQLite databases for an advanced course: chapter 16 of the 3rd edition and today's Python"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the textbook ontology built over the published chapter. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-01T12:00:00; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.4." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does chapter 16 of the 3rd edition teach about databases and the sqlite3 module, which of its printed outputs and programs still hold under Python 3.14.4 and SQLite 3.50.4, and what must an advanced course correct or add so that it matches current Python and SQLite?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-01." .
